<section class="section band">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">What it is</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Old habits, nothing to relearn.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">A file manager for people who navigate by keyboard and think in two panels.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid card-grid--features">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card-num">01</p>
        <h3 class="card-title">Two panels</h3>
        <p class="card-text">Source on the left, target on the right. Copy, move, pack and compare without opening a second window or reaching for the mouse.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card-num">02</p>
        <h3 class="card-title">Keyboard first</h3>
        <p class="card-text">Function keys along the bottom edge, a shortcut for everything, and a command line that stays exactly where your hands already are.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card card--accent">
        <p class="card-num card-num--brand">03</p>
        <h3 class="card-title">Its own core</h3>
        <p class="card-text"><span class="mono">tandemcommander.exe</span> is a program with its own identity: own icon, own window titles, own settings — and a modern core built for Windows 11, with full Unicode and long paths throughout.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
